MVP Goal
    Create npkg as a neutral, template-ready ancestor of pfig
    Prove one end-to-end cycle:
        pfig → npkg (neutralized)
        npkg → new package (via transform)
        Apply one fix across lineage (manual or semi-assisted)

Guiding Principle
    Make one transform and one fix travel across one fork
    If that works:
        the system works

Phase 0: Ground Rules
    npkg has NO history from pfig
    npkg is not a tool yet (no CLI required)
    pfork does not exist yet (manual transforms allowed)
    Focus on filesystem + text transforms only
    No automation beyond simple scripts
    Prefer clarity over cleverness
    Everything must be explainable and repeatable by hand

Phase 1: Create npkg Repo (Clean Genesis)
    mkdir npkg
    cd npkg
    git init

    copy contents of pfig into npkg working tree
        do NOT copy .git directory

    initial commit:
        "genesis: seed from pfig snapshot"

    sanity checks:
        project builds
        tests run (if applicable)
        makefile works
        CLI executes (even if still named pfig at this stage)

Phase 2: De-PFIG (Neutralization Pass)
    goal:
        remove identity
        preserve structure and capability

    global string transforms:
        "pfig" → "{{pkg_name}}"
        "PFIG" → "{{PKG_NAME}}"

    filesystem transforms:
        rename directory:
            pfig/ → {{pkg_name}}/
        update all imports accordingly

    CLI + entry points:
        replace command names with "{{pkg_name}}"
        update console_scripts in pyproject.toml

    metadata neutralization:
        pyproject.toml:
            name = "{{pkg_name}}"
            description templated or generic
        README.md:
            remove narrative specifics
            replace with placeholders
        manpages:
            convert to symbol-driven or placeholder form

    documentation + symbols:
        audit symbol table
        retain:
            code.meta.*
            project.*
            dynamic.*
        remove or generalize:
            pfig-specific narrative or tone
        ensure docs render with placeholders

    sweep for hard-coded assumptions:
        file paths
        environment variables
        command names

    commit:
        "transform: neutralize pfig → template variables"

Phase 3: Extract vs Embed Core Systems
    systems under consideration:
        guppy
        signals
        d2d

    MVP decision:
        DO NOT extract yet

    instead:
        treat as base capability of npkg template

    rationale:
        reduces moving parts
        avoids premature modularization
        keeps first transform simple

    annotate code:
        mark clearly:
            "candidate for future extraction"

    commit:
        "chore: mark core systems for future extraction"

Phase 4: Define First Transform (Manual)
    create directory:
        transforms/

    create file:
        rename_pkg.sh (or rename_pkg.toml)

    purpose:
        define transformation:
            {{pkg_name}} → concrete name (e.g. crinkle)

    scope:
        paths
        imports
        CLI entry points
        docs
        metadata

    implementation:
        start as bash + sed pipeline
        keep brutally simple and explicit

    requirement:
        must be:
            readable
            replayable
            reversible in principle

    commit:
        "transform: define pkg rename operation"

Phase 5: Instantiate First Derived Package
    from npkg:
        copy working tree → ../crinkle

    apply transform:
        run rename_pkg transform manually

    verify:
        project installs
        CLI works under new name
        docs render correctly
        no residual {{pkg_name}} in runtime paths

    commit in crinkle:
        "init: derived from npkg via rename transform"

Phase 6: Introduce a Fix
    in crinkle:
        modify behavior in a small, clear location
            example:
                logging tweak
                signal addition
                small bug fix

    document fix:
        fixes/
            fix_logging.txt (or .toml)

    manually propagate:
        identify equivalent location in npkg
        apply same logical change

    goal:
        demonstrate:
            transform reversal works conceptually
            fix can be re-applied upstream

    commits:
        npkg:
            "fix: logging improvement (from crinkle)"
        crinkle:
            "fix: logging improvement"

Phase 7: Define Minimal Metadata (Proto-PFork)
    create directory:
        .npkg/

    create file:
        lineage.toml

    contents:
        base = "../npkg"
        transforms = ["rename_pkg"]
        hop_count = 1

    purpose:
        record intent only
        no automation yet

    commit:
        "meta: record lineage and transforms"

Phase 8: Sanity Check Loop
    verify manually:
        can describe transforms clearly
        can reapply transforms by hand
        can map files across repos confidently
        can explain where a fix should land

    if yes:
        MVP achieved

    if no:
        simplify transforms further

Non-Goals (MVP)
    no pfork CLI
    no transform engine
    no dependency resolution for fixes
    no feature system
    no GitHub integration
    no branch combinatorics

Next Steps (Post-MVP)
    formalize transform spec (TOML vs script)
    build pfork apply/reverse engine
    introduce fix dependency tracking
    experiment with feature branches as template variants

Core Insight
    transforms preserve identity across structure
    fixes propagate behavior across lineage
    features define new branches of opinion

    keep these separate or the system collapses
